.TH EXTERNAL-DNS-DNSMASQ-WEBHOOK 8 "September 2026" "external-dns-dnsmasq-webhook" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
external-dns-dnsmasq-webhook \- ExternalDNS webhook provider for dnsmasq
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B external-dns-dnsmasq-webhook
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B external-dns-dnsmasq-webhook
implements version 1 of the ExternalDNS webhook API. It persists managed A,
AAAA, and CNAME records, renders them into a dedicated dnsmasq configuration
file, validates the complete dnsmasq configuration, and restarts dnsmasq.
Failed updates are rolled back.
.PP
All configuration is supplied through environment variables. The packaged
systemd unit reads the distribution's configuration file from
.IR /etc/default/external-dns-dnsmasq-webhook
or
.IR /etc/sysconfig/external-dns-dnsmasq-webhook .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DNSMASQ_WEBHOOK_LISTEN_ADDRESS
IP address and TCP port on which the webhook listens.
.TP
.B DNSMASQ_WEBHOOK_ALLOWED_CIDRS
Comma-separated client networks permitted to call the webhook.
.TP
.B DNSMASQ_WEBHOOK_DOMAIN
DNS suffix the provider is authorized to manage.
.TP
.B DNSMASQ_WEBHOOK_STATE_FILE
Persistent JSON provider state file.
.TP
.B DNSMASQ_WEBHOOK_CONFIG_FILE
Generated dnsmasq configuration file.
.TP
.B DNSMASQ_WEBHOOK_DNSMASQ_BINARY
Absolute path to dnsmasq.
.TP
.B DNSMASQ_WEBHOOK_SYSTEMCTL_BINARY
Absolute path to systemctl.
.TP
.B DNSMASQ_WEBHOOK_DNSMASQ_SERVICE
Name of the dnsmasq systemd unit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/external-dns-dnsmasq-webhook
Required site configuration on Debian-family systems.
.TP
.I /etc/sysconfig/external-dns-dnsmasq-webhook
Required site configuration on RPM-family systems.
.TP
.I /etc/dnsmasq.d/90-kubernetes-external-dns.conf
Static include for the generated records.
.TP
.I /var/lib/external-dns-dnsmasq-webhook/records.conf
Last-known-good generated dnsmasq records.
.TP
.I /var/lib/external-dns-dnsmasq-webhook/records.json
Persistent provider state.
.SH SECURITY
The webhook has no application-layer authentication. Bind it only to a trusted
interface and restrict TCP access with the host firewall. The provider also
enforces the configured source CIDRs and managed domain.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dnsmasq (8),
.BR external-dns (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
